  "description": "Runtime.callFunctionOn against an element objectId: Runtime.evaluate returns the button's RemoteObject (no returnByValue, so an objectId), then callFunctionOn invokes a function with `this` bound to that element which clicks it and returns its data-token. Verifies the click really fired (window.__btnClicks incremented) and the function return value came back. Anchors Runtime.callFunctionOn as the Moli non-coordinate action path (survey README fix #5).",
  "driver": {
    "kind": "raw_cdp",
    "steps": [
      {
        "method": "Runtime.evaluate",
        "params": {
          "expression": "document.getElementById('btn')"
        },
        "save_result_as": "elbtn"
      },
      {
        "method": "Runtime.callFunctionOn",
        "params": {
          "functionDeclaration": "function(){ this.click(); return this.getAttribute('data-token'); }",
          "objectId": "{saved:elbtn.result.objectId}",
          "returnByValue": true
